    "Noise: %lld%%" : {

    },
    "None of these theories can be proven. None can be fully disproven. That's what makes them theories.\n\nBut here's what they ALL share: they suggest that reality is not what it appears to be. That there's more going on than what your five senses report. That consciousness — YOUR consciousness — might be far more fundamental to the universe than you've been told.\n\nYour Prussian education taught you that you're a random accident on a random rock in a random universe, and that consciousness is just neurons firing.\n\nBut the greatest philosophers, physicists, and mystics across every civilization and every era have said: actually, it might be the other way around. Consciousness might come first. Reality might emerge from mind, not mind from reality.\n\nYou don't have to believe any of this. You just have to be willing to QUESTION. Because questioning is the first step out of the simulation — whether that simulation is digital, cultural, or neurological.\n\nWelcome to the deeper game. 🫠☀️" : {

    },
    "NONE YET" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "NINGUNO AÚN"
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "NINGUNO AÚN"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Not a shadow council - just incentives, cognitive biases, and institutions protecting themselves. Here's how they work." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No un consejo en la sombra - solo incentivos, sesgos cognitivos e instituciones protegiéndose a sí mismas. Así es como funcionan."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No un consejo en la sombra - solo incentivos, sesgos cognitivos e instituciones protegiéndose a sí mismas. Así es como funcionan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Not all gospels were written to be read by the masses. Some were written and THAT is why they were hidden. The teachings of Thomas, Mary Magdalene, Philip, and Judas didn't preach obedience — they preached awakening." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No todos los evangelios fueron escritos para ser leídos por las masas. Algunos fueron escritos y POR ESO fueron ocultados. Las enseñanzas de Tomás, María Magdalena, Felipe y Judas no predicaban obediencia — predicaban despertar."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No todos los evangelios fueron escritos para ser leídos por las masas. Algunos fueron escritos y POR ESO fueron ocultados. Las enseñanzas de Tomás, María Magdalena, Felipe y Judas no predicaban obediencia — predicaban despertar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Not all gospels were written to be read.\nSome were written — and that is why they were hidden." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No todos los evangelios fueron escritos para ser leídos.\nAlgunos fueron escritos — y por eso fueron ocultados."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No todos los evangelios fueron escritos para ser leídos.\nAlgunos fueron escritos — y por eso fueron ocultados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Not at all" : {

    },
    "Not enemies.\nNeighbors who were tricked into fighting." : {

    },
    "Not every conversation is worth engaging. Exit when:\n• Emotional tone escalates regardless of what you say\n• The same trigger word repeats after you've asked for specificity\n• The goal is clearly performance, not communication\n• Aggression increases when you demonstrate knowledge\n\nThe exit line: \"I see it differently. I don't think we'll resolve this right now — but I appreciate you sharing your perspective.\"" : {

    },
    "Not everyone claiming to be 'independent' is trustworthy. Watch out for:" : {
